# Build output.
#
# These are anchored with a leading slash so they match ONLY at the repo root.
# An unanchored "obj/" matches a directory named obj at ANY depth, which also
# swallows data/obj/ - the sample meshes (bunny, teapot, skull...). That is
# exactly how they went missing from the reconstructed history.
/obj/
*.o
/editor
/editor.exe

# Test binaries.
#
# A pattern rather than a line per suite. The per-test list below worked while
# suites arrived one at a time; three landed at once (bvh_test,
# import_curve_test, viewport_test) and all three were untracked and about to
# be committed as ~11 MB binaries. The individual entries that follow are now
# redundant, and harmless.
#
# Anchored, so it cannot match a source file: the suites' sources live in
# tests/ and keep their .cpp extension.
/*_test
/*_test.exe

# Test binaries
/bench
/bench.exe
/raytrace_test
/raytrace_test.exe
/demo_render
/demo_render.exe
/scene_test
/scene_test.exe
/animation_test
/animation_test.exe
/custom_shape_test
/custom_shape_test.exe
/render_section_test
/render_section_test.exe
/dirty_state_test
/dirty_state_test.exe
/specular_through_glass
/specular_through_glass.exe
/ice_scene
/ice_scene.exe
/ice_checker_scene
/ice_checker_scene.exe
/ice_render
/ice_render.exe
/refraction_acne
/refraction_acne.exe
/transform_test
/transform_test.exe
/obj_parser_test
/obj_parser_test.exe
/keyframe_test
/keyframe_test.exe
/texture_test
/texture_test.exe
/texture_scene
/texture_scene.exe
/curves_test
/curves_test.exe
/skinning_test
/skinning_test.exe

# Compiled libraries (source lives in src/vecmath)
*.a
*.so

# Runtime / editor state
/imgui.ini
/error_log.txt

# Generated scenes.
#
# ice_scene.cpp and ice_checker_scene.cpp WRITE these on every run -- they were
# committed for months as stale build output. scenes/showcase.scene is the
# opposite case and IS tracked: tests/demo_scenes.cpp generates it, but a
# student who never runs that tool still needs it in their clone.
/scenes/ice-block.scene
/scenes/ice-block-checker.scene

# Rendered output from the ray tracer.
#
# Broad on purpose: the Save-image dialog defaults to render.bmp but accepts
# any name you type, so there is no finite list of output filenames to
# enumerate. Sample textures live under data/textures/ and are exempted below.
*.ppm
*.bmp
!data/textures/
!data/textures/*.bmp


# Local backup clutter
/_archive/
*.bak
*.orig
Makefile.[0-9]
*.zip

# OS junk
.DS_Store
._*
Thumbs.db

#Local config file
editor.cfg
WiVRn/
